		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4Ten thousand is just a number until you start counting the footsteps, the growls, the hisses in the dark. This isn’t about a single beast, but about endurance, about showing up to every skirmish, every ambush, every siege, and walking away one more time. Each mob we fell leaves another mark on our armor and our minds, tiny stories written in cuts and cracks. By the time we reach that number, we won’t be the same people who started this tally."]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "6CF620CBAD48D019"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1ADD9A957F817717"
				item: "chipped:tropics_melon"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "75239C01EAD2F634"
				stat: "minecraft:mob_kills"
				type: "stat"
				value: 10000
			}]
			title: "Ten Thousand Kills"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4There’s a kind of madness in a task like this, how much punishment a body can endure before it simply doesn’t anymore. We’ve learned to read our scars like pages in a book: burns from blaze fire, jagged gouges from creepers, neat punctures from skeleton arrows. Twelve thousand hurts is less about bravery and more about stubbornness, about standing back up when anyone sane would stay down. If we live through it, we’ll know exactly where our limits used to be."]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "236CDF4D91BC9948"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "2339CB9DED6DE4D1"
					item: "minecraft:enchanted_golden_apple"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
